  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "FULL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 5.0,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-NS-24: 5.00 SGD goodwill credit to the rider — the driver failed to arrive at the pickup by the scheduled time plus five minutes and also failed to attempt contact before cancelling."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "Both parties: I have gone through the trip record, the driver's GPS trace, the chat log, the payments ledger and both profiles. The 5.00 SGD cancellation fee charged at 16:09:34 (EV-FARE-06056) does not stand, for two independent reasons, so the rider is refunded in full.\n\n1) POL-NS-23 — the driver's contact obligation. Before cancelling for a no-show the driver must have sent at least one in-app chat message AND placed at least one in-app call, both before the cancellation. The complete trip record (EV-TRIP-06056, weight 1.0) reports contact_before_cancel.call_count = 0 and message_count = 0, and the complete chat log (EV-CHAT-06056, weight 1.0) holds only two messages, both sent by the rider (16:02:00 and 16:05:30). The single in-app call on the trip was placed by the rider at 16:06:10 and went unanswered. Either limb missing voids the fee; both are missing. The fee is therefore voided, the rider is not charged, and there is no driver compensation.\n\n2) POL-NS-24 — the driver never reached the pickup. The 15:58:10 arrival tap is not corroborated by the trace, and the category's arrival test reads the tap only where the GPS corroborates it within the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius. On the complete, gap-free driver trace (EV-GPS-06056, weight 1.0) the closest fix is 364.96 m from Block 520 (accuracy 9.0 m), and the vehicle stands still at that same spot from 15:58:00 to the 16:09:30 cancellation. The driver did not arrive by the 16:05:00 deadline, so no fee may be charged and the 5.00 SGD is refunded in full. The record's 'arrived_by_deadline = true' reads the button press alone; a status a party sets records only that it was set, and it does not establish presence at the pickup.\n\nOn the driver's submissions: he did sit stationary for the whole wait, as the trace shows, and the fee amount does match the 5.00 SGD policy figure — but the trace puts that stop 364.96 m from the pickup, not at it, and the record shows no contact attempt, so the DRIVER_COMPENSATION outcome of POL-NS-22 is not reached. The rider's own messages and call show he was on the app and engaged, which is consistent with a passenger waiting; it does not rescue a cancellation taken without arrival or contact. The absent traffic advisory (EV-ADVIS-06056-01, MISSING, weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT) carries no fact and supplies no traffic excuse.\n\nBecause the driver both failed to arrive by the deadline and failed to attempt contact, POL-NS-24 additionally gives the rider a 5.00 SGD goodwill credit. Under POL-GEN-03 that is a referral riding alongside the refund, not part of amount_sgd, so the refund stays at the 5.00 SGD actually charged.\n\nNo escalation applies. The facts POL-NS-23 and POL-NS-24 turn on are carried by complete, unimpaired artifacts, so POL-GEN-26 has no open question to act on. There is no safety flag (POL-GEN-21) and no fraud flag on either profile (POL-GEN-22, fraud_flags = 0). The dispute value is 5.00 SGD, below 10.00 SGD, so the AI ruling is final at any confidence (POL-GEN-22, POL-NS-26). No repeat no-show referral arises: the POL-NS-25 counter is absent from the rider profile, and in any event the fee does not stand so the count cannot move.\n\nOutcome for the rider, who filed: FULL_REFUND of the whole contested 5.00 SGD, with no driver compensation.",
    "amount_sgd_note": null
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "FULL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 5.0,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-NS-24: the rider is due a 5.00 SGD goodwill credit, because the driver failed to arrive at the pickup location by the scheduled pickup time plus 5 minutes (16:00:00 + 5 min = 16:05:00) and also failed to attempt contact before cancelling."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "Rider, your claim succeeds. Driver, the 5.00 SGD no-show fee does not stand. Two independent grounds void it, and both rest on complete artifacts at weight 1.0.\n\nFirst, the contact obligation (POL-NS-23). Before cancelling for a no-show the driver must have sent the rider at least one in-app chat message AND placed at least one in-app call, both before the 16:09:30 cancellation. The complete chat log (EV-CHAT-06056) holds exactly two messages, MSG-06056-001 and MSG-06056-002, and the sender on both is RIDER — the driver sent nothing. The trip record's in-app call list (EV-TRIP-06056) records no call from the driver; the single call at 16:06:10 was placed by the rider and rang 25 s unanswered. Both limbs fail, so under POL-NS-23 the fee is voided and the rider is not charged: FULL_REFUND of the 5.00 SGD actually charged (EV-FARE-06056, total_charged 5.00, refund_issued_sgd 0.0), with no driver compensation.\n\nSecond, arrival (POL-NS-24 with the category's arrival test). The driver's 15:58:10 'arrived' entry is a button the driver pressed (source PLATFORM_TELEMETRY); the category test asks whether that arrival event is corroborated by the GPS trace within the arrival radius. The complete, gap-free device trace (EV-GPS-06056, weight 1.0, 50 fixes, coverage 100%, max gap 30 s) does not corroborate it: the nearest fix is 364.96 m from Block 520 with 9.0 m reported accuracy, far outside the 50 m STANDARD radius, and the vehicle then sat at that spot at speed 0 until the 16:09:30 cancellation. The driver therefore never reached the pickup by the 16:05:00 deadline, so the fee charged is refunded in full; and because he also failed to attempt contact, POL-NS-24 adds the 5.00 SGD goodwill credit recorded in the referrals above.\n\nOn the driver's points: the free-wait timing under POL-NS-21 is met (driver arrived before the 16:00 schedule, so the 300 s wait ran from 16:00 and expired at 16:05:00, before the 16:09:30 cancellation), and the amount charged equals the 5.00 SGD policy fee under POL-NS-22 (fee_matches_policy true, fee_charged_sgd 5.00), so there is no fee-amount defect and no POL-NS-22 referral — but correct timing and the correct amount do not save a fee that POL-NS-23 and POL-NS-24 void, so no DRIVER_COMPENSATION arises. The claim that the record's arrived_by_deadline is true, and the driver's statement that he waited at the pickup, are outweighed by the driver's own device trace: the stationary dwell (POL-NS-21) is real, but it is 364.96 m from the pickup point, so it does not show he waited there. The missing traffic advisory (EV-ADVIS-06056-01, weight 0.0, MISSING_ARTIFACT) carries no fact for either side and supplies no excuse. Because the facts POL-NS-23 and POL-NS-24 turn on are carried by COMPLETE, issue-free, weight-1.0 artifacts, no needed fact is missing and POL-GEN-26 does not escalate. No repeat no-show flag arises under POL-NS-25: the rider's no-show counter is 0 and the fee does not stand.\n\nAmount: 5.00 SGD returned to the rider — the whole contested sum, read from the fare breakdown (fee_charged_sgd 5.00, refund_if_voided_sgd 5.00). Confidence 0.9, within the cap of 1.0 set by the deciding artifacts (EV-CHAT-06056, EV-TRIP-06056, EV-GPS-06056, all 1.0). The dispute value is 5.00 SGD, below POL-GEN-22's 10.00 SGD band, and neither party carries a fraud flag, so under POL-GEN-22 and POL-NS-26 this AI ruling is final."
  },
